      "en": "In Morocco's parliamentary review of Finance Bill No. 60.26, Article 36 officially proposes raising the legal ceiling for multi-year advance commitments by the National Defense Administration to MAD 190.5 billion (~USD 19.4B / EUR 17.3B). This marks a 21.2% hike over the MAD 157.17B ceiling in 2026. The expanded authorization enables the Moroccan government to sign long-cycle multi-billion-dollar foreign procurement contracts for strategic air defense, precision strike missiles, and domestic defense manufacturing with disbursements spread across future fiscal cycles.",
